1. final Keyword
final is a keyword used to restrict modification.

It can be applied to:

Variable

Method

Class

Parameters

Local Variables

Reference Variables

A. Final Variable
A final variable can be assigned only once.

class Demo {

    final int x = 10;

    void display() {
        // x = 20; // Compile-time Error
    }
}
Output

Compile-time Error
cannot assign a value to final variable x
Blank Final Variable
Can be initialized inside constructor.

class Student {

    final int rollNo;

    Student(int rollNo){
        this.rollNo = rollNo;
    }

    void display(){
        System.out.println(rollNo);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args){

        Student s1 = new Student(101);
        Student s2 = new Student(102);

        s1.display();
        s2.display();
    }
}
Output

101
102
Every object can initialize it once.

Static Blank Final Variable
Must be initialized inside static block.

class Demo{

    static final int x;

    static{
        x = 100;
    }

    public static void main(String args[]){
        System.out.println(x);
    }
}
Output

100
